  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Binomial Expansions: approximating a power of a number just below 1</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 1.2: Write a number just below 1 as 1 + x with x negative, and estimate its power from four terms of (1 + x)^n to 4 decimal places.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 5, Section A, Exercise A, question 4(c) of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 2 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: new numbers and powers, randomised; x is found first and the estimate is given to 4 decimal places.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
